Z||000000||Loki||03-09-2001||01:40 PM||||OK,  Im trying to take the outter door skin off to make it easier to replace to door lock cylinder and looks like 2 of the little rubber things that hold the skin to the door are stripped.... How do I get those off? Any help please.<P><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki137/loki5.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/headshot.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||03-09-2001||03:15 PM||||try using vise grips around the outside.  You'll chew the heck out of them, but they will probably come off.  Make sure to use a lot of WD-40 too.  If you can't find replacements, Rodney Dickman sells new door skin screws.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||JetroGT||03-09-2001||08:14 PM||||I used a hammer and a chizel. Taped around the edge. Or you can cut the top layer of plastic off to get to the real metal torx.||||reg||1
